    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Antibes and Juan-les-Pins area has many accommodations open to dogs — without any single address that really stands out from the rest. Several Sandaya-chain campsites in the area accept animals, as do most of the hotels in Juan-les-Pins.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Unlike other addresses in this guide where conditions are clearly stated, those in Antibes vary a lot from one establishment to another — dog size, breed, possible surcharge. The most reliable approach is to call directly before booking, rather than relying solely on booking site filters.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Cap d'Antibes coastal path makes for a lovely leashed walk during the stay.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>L'Hippodrome beach in Cagnes-sur-Mer and Vaugrenier beach in Villeneuve-Loubet are the closest dog-friendly swimming options.</p>
